{
    "word": "gaydar",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c997b106-55e9-3c42-ab16-3d0165b4b1bf",
                "word": "gaydar",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ceef7ab0-f463-4a29-905c-4ed2938491ba",
                        "entry_id": "c997b106-55e9-3c42-ab16-3d0165b4b1bf",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "gaydars"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "76af7d1d-a7a7-3b0d-abbd-a84702b03ca6",
                        "entry_id": "c997b106-55e9-3c42-ab16-3d0165b4b1bf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The supposed ability to detect whether or not a person is gay by observing that person's appearance, mannerisms, etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a90aed6e-cfd0-4d59-8f8a-6ba543a1ef9a",
                                "sense_id": "76af7d1d-a7a7-3b0d-abbd-a84702b03ca6",
                                "text": "This is not your Hallmark in Ames, Iowa. And there is “family” working there … no radar like gaydar, I always say."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "84ed9f18-06f3-49bf-8a84-998fc4b0cd30",
                                "sense_id": "76af7d1d-a7a7-3b0d-abbd-a84702b03ca6",
                                "text": "When you first come out, you might have an overactive gaydar. When I realized I was gay, I wanted everyone to be gay too, which led to a lot of wishful thinking. \"Helen Hunt is gay!\" Dream on, girl!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2bfcef49-b9b2-46d0-ac8e-667f568becf9",
                                "sense_id": "76af7d1d-a7a7-3b0d-abbd-a84702b03ca6",
                                "text": "\"I dunno. He's carried this one on since Halloween. I'm starting to think the lie was actually the 'straight guy role'. I may have a crappy gaydar, but having faked heterosexuality before, I feel like I should be able to recognize it.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b90ed145-34f4-42ef-b148-98402313c317",
                                "sense_id": "76af7d1d-a7a7-3b0d-abbd-a84702b03ca6",
                                "text": "The research, which went viral this week, used a sample of online dating photos, limited only to white users, to demonstrate that an algorithm could correctly distinguish between gay and straight men 81% of the time and 74% for women, suggesting machines can potentially have much better \"gaydar\" than humans."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d3ca4d30-5f5c-43b4-b7af-656a4da78355",
                                "sense_id": "76af7d1d-a7a7-3b0d-abbd-a84702b03ca6",
                                "text": "Dr. Lillihammer started to walk past her, but stopped directly in front of her. Inches apart, they stared at each other. Sizing the other woman up, doing a little consulting of their gaydars. Heather felt Lillian's breath on her cheek and tried not to visibly let the shiver go down her spine."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "90a5f8ed-a4a8-41d9-84d8-7f47b4f4c1c6",
                        "source_entry_id": "c997b106-55e9-3c42-ab16-3d0165b4b1bf",
